{"id": "westside-pump-station-bid-outreach", "title": "Why San Francisco rejected the lowest Westside Pump Station bid", "seconds": 44.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "2da48356b1e7d762", "words": 128, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "Ten firms applied for prequalification. Eight qualified, and three bid.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.29, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Why", "did", "the", "lowest", "bid", "lose?"], "sub": "Westside pump station"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.48, 0.77, 0.92, 2.23, 2.48, 3.35, 3.52, 3.78]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "The project required a 15 percent subcontracting share for certified local small and micro businesses.", "t0": 4.41, "t1": 9.36, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bid", "kicker": "San Francisco Public Utilities Commission", "text": "2020 solicitation", "mark": "2020 solicitation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.48, 0.85, 0.93, 1.32, 1.67, 2.39, 2.64, 2.8, 3.26, 3.57, 3.87, 3.96, 4.27]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The underlying local business ordinance dated to 2006.", "t0": 9.48, "t1": 12.5, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "law", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors", "text": "2006 ordinance", "mark": "2006 ordinance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.58, 0.83, 1.16, 1.55, 1.9, 2.0, 2.18, 2.53]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "Thompson Builders submitted the lowest price.", "t0": 12.62, "t1": 14.72, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "tab", "kicker": "San Francisco Public Utilities Commission", "text": "Bid results", "mark": "Bid results"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.83, 1.2, 1.3, 1.59]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "Anvil and Western Water protested. The City requested more information.", "t0": 14.84, "t1": 18.84, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "relationship", "context": "After the bids", "heading": "Who challenged whom", "source": "minutes", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Anvil and Western Water", "value": "Protested Thompson"}, {"icon": "audit", "label": "Contract Monitoring Division", "value": "Sought more information"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.51, 0.86, 1.15, 2.25, 2.43, 2.71, 3.15, 3.32]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "The City found Thompson’s bid nonresponsive on outreach grounds.", "t0": 18.96, "t1": 22.06, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Good-faith outreach"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.37, 0.64, 1.1, 1.37, 2.07, 2.19, 2.55]}, {"scene": "decision", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "Thompson challenged the review. City staff said both bidders could supplement their records.", "t0": 22.28, "t1": 26.79, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "minutes", "kicker": "San Francisco Public Utilities Commission", "text": "Commission minutes", "mark": "Commission minutes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.81, 0.92, 1.82, 2.12, 2.43, 2.63, 2.86, 3.21, 3.39, 3.82, 4.0]}, {"scene": "decision", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "A separate protest of Anvil's qualifications was denied.", "t0": 26.91, "t1": 29.53, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Separate protest"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.45, 0.9, 1.01, 1.33, 2.02, 2.15]}, {"scene": "decision", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[4]"], "text": "In February 2021, the Commission awarded the contract to Anvil.", "t0": 29.65, "t1": 33.37, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$48,328,300", "label": "Award to Anvil Builders"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.64, 0.89, 1.54, 1.7, 2.23, 2.62, 2.73, 3.19, 3.31]}, {"scene": "decision", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "A later audit found protests on 14 of 124 contracts it examined.", "t0": 33.49, "t1": 37.35, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "audit", "kicker": "San Francisco Budget and Legislative Analyst", "text": "Review of Chapter 6 contracts", "mark": "Review of Chapter 6 contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 0.69, 0.89, 1.3, 1.43, 1.83, 1.93, 2.08, 2.31, 2.74, 3.24, 3.35]}, {"scene": "decision", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The award amount alone does not establish a price premium or improper preference.", "t0": 37.47, "t1": 41.46, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Price premium", "Improper preference"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.72, 1.14, 1.31, 1.47, 1.89, 1.96, 2.26, 2.74, 2.91, 3.36]}, {"scene": "decision", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 41.58, "t1": 43.72, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.65, 0.8, 1.06, 1.17, 1.26, 1.5, 1.76]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The pump station bids", "decision": "The award"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "question"}